{"id":552084316,"iid":4157,"project_id":34675721,"title":"fix(artifact-registry): write sbt credentials for both sbt 1.x and 2.x","description":"## What does this MR do and why?\n\n`glab artifact-registry login --sbt` now writes the credential to both the sbt 1.x and the sbt 2.x global base, so a build on either version authenticates after the command reports success.\n\nBefore this MR it wrote only `~/.sbt/1.0/credentials.sbt`. sbt picks the global base from the `sbt.version` a project declares in `project/build.properties`, and sbt 2.x never reads the 1.x base. A project on sbt 2.x therefore failed with `unauthorized` after a successful login.\n\nThis is step 2 of https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/ops/artifact-registry/-/work_items/1083 (acceptance criteria 4 and 5).\n\n- `sbtCredentialsFilesFor` resolves the 2.x base the way `SysProp.defaultGlobalBaseDirectory` does in [sbt 2.0.8](https://github.com/sbt/sbt/blob/v2.0.8/main/src/main/scala/sbt/internal/SysProp.scala#L209-L225): `$SBT_CONFIG_HOME`, then `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sbt` (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\sbt` on Windows), then `~/.config/sbt`, each with `2/credentials.sbt` appended. Values are trimmed, as sbt trims them.\n- The success line names each file and the sbt version that reads it. `--sbt` usage and `--help` say the same, and the \"assumes a stock sbt 1.x\" caveat is gone.\n- When the 2.x write fails after the 1.x write succeeds, the command fails and names the file it did write.\n\nTwo places where this differs from #1083's wording:\n\n- **Windows.** The issue lists `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` for every platform. sbt 2.0.8 reads `LOCALAPPDATA` on Windows instead, so this MR does too.\n- **Relative paths.** sbt resolves a relative value against the directory the build runs in. `glab` cannot know that directory, so it skips a relative value, as the [XDG Base Directory spec](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/latest/#variables) requires, and falls through to the next one.\n\n## How to verify\n\nVerified on staging (`artifact-registry.staging.gitlab.com`, `ar-registry/conformance-maven`) with `sbt -batch update` and the Coursier cache cleared before each run (criterion 8 of #1083). With both files written by this branch, sbt 2.0.8 and 1.10.7 both resolve. With only the 1.x file, sbt 2.0.8 fails `unauthorized`. With only the 2.x file, sbt 1.10.7 fails `unauthorized`.\n\nThe table below repeats those runs, and adds the environment-variable cases, against a localhost stub. The stub answers `401` with `Basic realm=\"artifact-registry\"` unless the request carries `__token__` and the exact token `glab` wrote.\n\n| Files present | `sbt.version=2.0.8` | `sbt.version=1.10.7` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Both, written by this branch | `[success]` | `[success]` |\n| 1.x file only (behavior before this MR) | `unauthorized` | not run |\n| 2.x file only | not run | `unauthorized` |\n| 2.x file under an absolute `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` | `[success]` | not run |\n| 2.x file under an absolute `SBT_CONFIG_HOME` | `[success]` | not run |\n| Relative `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` (`glab` writes `~/.config/sbt/2`) | `unauthorized` | not run |\n\nThe last row is the expected limitation. sbt 2 read `\u003cproject\u003e/relcfg/sbt/2` there.\n\nUnit tests cover the base resolution order (including Windows, trimming, and relative values), writing both files, and both partial-failure orders.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","state":"opened","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:29:42.044Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T16:22:48.086Z","merged_by":null,"merge_user":null,"merged_at":null,"closed_by":null,"closed_at":null,"target_branch":"main","source_branch":"ar-1083-sbt-both-global-bases","user_notes_count":9,"upvotes":0,"downvotes":0,"author":{"id":27667902,"username":"sylviashen","public_email":"","name":"Sylvia Shen","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/27667902/avatar.png?v=1792498380","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/sylviashen","bot":false},"assignees":[{"id":27667902,"username":"sylviashen","public_email":"","name":"Sylvia Shen","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/27667902/avatar.png?v=1792498380","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/sylviashen"}],"assignee":{"id":27667902,"username":"sylviashen","public_email":"","name":"Sylvia Shen","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/27667902/avatar.png?v=1792498380","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/sylviashen"},"reviewers":[{"id":5054840,"username":"jdrpereira","public_email":"","name":"João Pereira","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/5054840/avatar.png?v=1792507392","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/jdrpereira"},{"id":12347103,"username":"arpitgogia","public_email":"","name":"Arpit Gogia","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/12347103/avatar.png?v=1792522528","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/arpitgogia"},{"id":21826781,"username":"GitLabDuo","public_email":null,"name":"GitLab Duo","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/GitLabDuo"}],"source_project_id":34675721,"target_project_id":34675721,"labels":["Category:Artifact Registry","artifact-registry::cli","bug::functional","devops::package","group::package registry","priority::2","section::ci","severity::3","type::bug","workflow::in review"],"draft":false,"imported":false,"imported_from":"none","work_in_progress":false,"milestone":null,"merge_when_pipeline_succeeds":false,"merge_status":"can_be_merged","detailed_merge_status":"requested_changes","merge_after":null,"sha":"25892092f1db0711fcea689c27db39f6d928d2eb","merge_commit_sha":null,"squash_commit_sha":null,"discussion_locked":null,"should_remove_source_branch":null,"force_remove_source_branch":true,"prepared_at":"2026-10-20T12:29:59.075Z","referen